.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-ADD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-add - Print Linux/macOS and Windows machine enrollment commands


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine add [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print Linux/macOS and Windows machine enrollment commands

.PP
Create an enrollment command for Linux, macOS, or Windows and optionally give the new machine a name. The printed one-shot material should be used on the intended machine.

.PP
Machines are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected machine, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	optional machine hostname


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
